      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. he definitely has that fire. but i want to make sure he doesn't just sound like a guy who's angry. i want him to sound like he actually has a logical, moral framework. \n\ncan you add a part to the monologue where he explains why the \"globalist\" view is fundamentally wrong or even dangerous? like, instead of just calling them names, have him explain why the philosophy of internationalism itself is a failure that's destroying the social fabric of the nation. make it sound like a deep, structural critique of how the world is run right now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
